==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|endictment}}

===Etymology===
18th-century Latinized respelling of {{inh|en|enm|endytement||action of accusing}}, from {{der|en|xno|enditement}}, from {{m|fro|enditer}}, from {{der|en|LL.|indictō|indictāre}}, from {{der|en|la|indictus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈdaɪt.mənt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-indictment.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} An official formal [[accusation]] for a criminal [[offence]], or the process by which it is brought to a [[jury]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The official legal document outlining the [[charge]]s concerned; bill of indictment. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=William K. Rashbaum|title=This is what will happen when Trump is arrested in the coming days.|work=The New York Times|date=2023-03-30|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/03/30/nyregion/indictment-meaning-trump-arrest.html|issn=0362-4331|passage={{...}}— the '''indictment''' will remain sealed until his expected arraignment on Tuesday, when the charges will be formally revealed.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} An [[accusation]] of wrongdoing; a [[criticism]] or [[condemnation]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
# Evidence of failure or poor performance.
#: {{ux|en|an '''indictment''' of his ability to lead}}
#: {{ux|en|an '''indictment''' of his game}}

